      "writtenOn": "2026-11-24T08:51:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes I will add a comment explaining this.\n\nExpired entries are another reason removal can return null.\n\n- `remove()`: If the entry has expired, Caffeine sets the removal cause to EXPIRED [1](https://github.com/ben-manes/caffeine/blob/v2.9.2/caffeine/src/main/java/com/github/benmanes/caffeine/cache/BoundedLocalCache.java#L2176-L2177).\n\n- `remove()`: removes it from the map [2](https://github.com/ben-manes/caffeine/blob/v2.9.2/caffeine/src/main/java/com/github/benmanes/caffeine/cache/BoundedLocalCache.java#L2181-L2185).\n\n- `remove()`: notifies the `onRemoval` listeners [3](https://github.com/ben-manes/caffeine/blob/v2.9.2/caffeine/src/main/java/com/github/benmanes/caffeine/cache/BoundedLocalCache.java#L2189-L2191).\n\n- `remove()`: returns the old value only when the cause is `EXPLICIT`. For EXPIRED, it returns `null` [4](https://github.com/ben-manes/caffeine/blob/v2.9.2/caffeine/src/main/java/com/github/benmanes/caffeine/cache/BoundedLocalCache.java#L2194)\n\nSo this means that if an entry has expired but is still stored internally when explicitly invalidated, it can produce two notifications:\n\n1. Caffeine sends `EXPIRED`.\n2. Our wrapper sends `EXPLICIT` because Caffeine returns `null`.\n\nThis is correct because the entry expiring locally does not mean it has expired on the other nodes. HA and multi-site ignore the EXPIRED notification, so the EXPLICIT notification is still needed to invalidate their copies.",
